# FirmShake design steering

Reference for product/UX decisions. Prefer extending these patterns over inventing alternatives unless requirements change.

## Message archival

**Model:** Per-user archive state on `users/{uid}/inboxState/{docId}` with `isArchived: boolean` and `archivedAt` timestamp. Doc IDs match thread keys via `inboxStateDocId(listingId, buyerId?)` — same IDs as inbox threads, not separate archive records.

**Why not on `threads` docs:** Archive is per-user. Storing on shared thread docs would require merge writes that risk overwriting other participants' fields. Subcollection under the user keeps writes isolated.

**Behavior:**
- New messages do **not** auto-unarchive. User must explicitly unarchive (overflow menu or message view).
- Toggle archive in place on **Buying**, **Selling**, and **Inbox** tabs — no dedicated archive routes.
- UI: `TabArchivedSection` — collapsed "See archived messages" button; expanded shows divider + header + archived rows.
  - Inbox: header **"Archived Messages"**
  - Buying / Selling: header **"Archived Items"**
- **Selling:** Only buyer threads are filtered by archive. Seller's own listings always stay in the main list; archived buyer conversations appear only in the archived section.

**Implementation:** `src/features/messages/services/inboxState.ts`, `TabArchivedSection.vue`, `ConversationOverflowMenu.vue`.

## Unread / "New" badge

Show **"New"** only when the thread has unread activity **and** `lastMessageSenderId !== currentUserId`.

**Rationale:** Messages the user just sent should not appear as unread to them. Archived threads never show as unread (`isThreadUnread` returns false when archived).

**Implementation:** `isThreadUnread()` in `inboxState.ts`; badge on Inbox rows and equivalent buying/selling thread rows.

## Blocked users

**Model:** Per-user block list at `users/{uid}/blockedUsers/{blockedUserId}` with `blockedAt` timestamp.

**Management UI:** Settings → **Blocked users** → `/blockedusers`. Live subscription to the block subcollection; display names via profile lookup (`useParticipantProfiles`).

**Block confirmation:** Before blocking, show `ion-alert` with message *"Blocking a user means you will no longer able to see their listing and restricts all communication. Do you still want to proceed?"* and **Yes** / **No**. Unblock from inline toggles (listing detail, messages) stays immediate — no confirmation.

**Block success banner:** After a successful block, show a top `ion-toast` (5s, dismissible): *"You have successfully blocked <name>. You can see all blocked users by going to Gear Icon -> Blocked Users"* using the blocked user's display name from participant profiles.

**Unblock confirmation:** On **Blocked Users** settings page only, show `ion-alert` with message *"The user will be unblocked, and each side can start communicating again. Would you like to proceed?"* and **Accept** / **Cancel**.

**Implementation:** `src/common/services/blocks.ts`, `src/common/services/blockUi.ts`, `BlockedUsersPage.vue`, `ListingDetailPage.vue`, `ListingMessagesPage.vue`, `ProfilePage.vue`.

## Password reset flow

**Do not use** Firebase `sendPasswordResetEmail`. Use **email link sign-in** (`sendSignInLinkToEmail` + `signInWithEmailLink`) so MFA-enrolled users can complete SMS verification before setting a new password.

**Flow:** Forgot password → email link → MFA challenge if enrolled → new password + confirm on `/reset-password` → **sign out** (user signs in fresh with new password).

**Firebase console:** Enable **Email link (passwordless sign-in)** under Authentication → Sign-in method (in addition to Email/Password).

**Client patterns** (match Firebase email-link docs):
- Store email in `localStorage` (`firmshake.emailForPasswordReset`); clear after successful link sign-in.
- Track pending flow in `sessionStorage` (`firmshake.passwordResetPending`).
- Continue URL: `${origin}/reset-password` via `getPasswordResetContinueUrl()`.
- reCAPTCHA gate before sending link.

**Implementation:** `src/features/auth/services/passwordReset.ts`, `ForgotPasswordPage.vue`, `ResetPasswordPage.vue`.

## Custom domain (`firm-shake.com`)

When adding or changing production domains:

| Surface | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Firebase Auth | Add `firm-shake.com` and `www.firm-shake.com` to **Authorized domains** |
| firmshake-api | `CORS_ORIGINS` must include both apex and `www` |
| Firebase Hosting | `/controlpanel` and `/controlpanel/*` redirect (301) to `https://firmshake-controlpanel.web.app/` — see `firebase.json` |

**Deploy:** Web/hosting changes → `npm run deploy:hosting` (see deploy rule). API CORS → `firmshake-api` staging deploy.

