## Guest / unauthenticated UX

**Root routing (`/`):**

| Platform | Guest destination |
|---|---|
| Desktop web | `/welcome` — 3-card FirmShake landing carousel |
| Mobile web | `/tabs/home` — guest browse (no forced landing) |
| Capacitor native | `/login` |

Signed-in users always land on `/tabs/home`.

**Landing (`/welcome`):** Three cards only — (1) community marketplace / FirmShake concept, (2) bounded meetups/price/agreements, (3) deposits + 50% compensation when broken. Arrow navigation + Get started / Browse listings / Sign in CTAs.

**Mobile web guests:** Bottom tabs show **Browse** + **Login/Create** only. Toolbar replaces profile/gear/notifications with **Login/Create**. Community segment hidden on Browse. Desktop guests browsing keep full tab bar; protected tabs still redirect to login.

**Guest browse promo (mobile):** Unauthenticated mobile browse shows a compact carousel (max **25vh**) above listings — same three FirmShake cards as `/welcome`, with arrow/swipe navigation. Shared copy in `landingCards.ts`; component `GuestBrowsePromo.vue`. **Sell on All** CTA hidden for guests. Filter hamburger sits inline with the search bar (not a separate row).

**Firestore reads:** Guests may read active listings, community feeds, categories, and communities (browse + listing detail). Writes remain auth-only.

**Implementation:** `src/utils/platform.ts`, `src/router/rootRoute.ts`, `LandingPage.vue`, `GuestBrowsePromo.vue`, `LoginCreatePage.vue`, `TabsPage.vue`, `AppTopToolbar.vue`, `HomePage.vue`, `appBootstrap.ts` (`startGuestBootstrap`).

## BFF browse search

**Primary path:** `POST /api/v1/browse/search` via `browseSearch.ts` when `useBffBrowse()` is true (default when API configured). Guest-accessible; optional Bearer token enables block-list filtering.

**Filter UX:**
- **Community tab:** instant search + `sessionStorage` persistence (`firmshake.browseCommunityId`) — not part of draft/Apply.
- **Combined Apply** (sidebar button): text search, category, price min/max, geo (center + radius mi), sort.
- **Draft vs applied:** sidebar/searchbar edit draft state; fetch uses applied state only after Apply (or community change).

**Search engine:** Typesense when `TYPESENSE_HOST` + `TYPESENSE_API_KEY` set on API; Firestore fallback in tests/dev. Location sync uses geopoint field `location: [lat, lng]` + `hasLocation` bool.

**Categories:** `GET /api/v1/categories?active=true` via `categoriesBff.ts` / `categoriesRouter.ts`. Seed data lives in API (`services/data/seed_categories.py` + `scripts/seed_categories.py`); client `ensureCategoriesSeeded()` skipped when BFF browse enabled.

**Pagination:** page-based `hasMore` from BFF (including geo-active searches). Legacy Firestore feed + client `applyBrowseListingFilters` only when `VITE_USE_BFF_BROWSE=false`.

**Sort options:** `newest`, `price_asc`, `price_desc`, `distance` (when geo applied).

**Map view:** List | Map toggle on Browse when BFF enabled; `BrowseMapView.vue` + `@googlemaps/markerclusterer`.

**Map distance filter:** Sidebar **Distance** radius (`BrowseGeoFilter`) drives map search when a geo center is applied — BFF requests use `appliedGeoFilter` lat/lng + `radiusMiles`; map fits bounds to that radius via `centerRadiusMiles`. Pan/zoom does **not** refetch while geo is active (viewport search applies only without an applied center). Map toolbar **Go to current location** / address search uses the sidebar radius and syncs draft + applied geo state. **Implementation:** `resolveMapSearchViewport()` in `browseMapView.ts`, `HomePage.vue` (`onGeoFilterApply`, `buildMapSearchParams`, `loadMapListings`). Map fetches up to **`BROWSE_MAP_MAX_PREFETCH_PAGES`** pages per viewport (100 listings/page) within the applied radius — not a global pin dump.

**Seller pin aggregation:** When one seller has multiple listings within **~105 ft** (`BROWSE_MAP_AGGREGATE_RADIUS_MILES`, 0.02 mi), the map shows **one green pin** with a count label instead of overlapping blue pins. Aggregation is **per seller only** — different sellers at the same coordinates stay separate; same seller at distant locations stay separate. Pin colors: **blue** (`#3880ff`) single listing, **green** (`#2dd36f`) aggregated. Click/hover opens a compact popup: single-item keeps the existing card; aggregated shows scrollable rows (thumbnail, title, price) linking to listing detail. Zoom-level `MarkerClusterer` still handles dense map areas. **BFF:** `POST /api/v1/browse/search` always returns `pinGroups[]` alongside listings; client uses `serverPinGroups` with client-side fallback. **Implementation:** `browse_map_pins.py` (API), `browseMapPinAggregation.ts`, `BrowseMapView.vue`.

**Multi-category:** API accepts `categoryIds[]` with OR semantics; UI single-select for now.

**Implementation:** `browseSearch.ts`, `categoriesBff.ts`, `browseCommunityStorage.ts`, `HomePage.vue`, `BrowseMapView.vue`, firmshake-api `services/browse_search.py`, `routes/v1/browse.py`.

## Settings navigation

**Terminology:** User-facing label is **Settings** (document title `firm-shake - Settings`). Route path stays `/tabs/profile`; internal route name `Profile`.

**Header:** Toolbar avatar is display-only. **Settings** gear icon between avatar and notifications bell navigates to the settings page (`ProfilePage.vue`).

**Mobile toolbar (≤768px):** Title stacks two lines (`FirmShake -` / page name); display name hidden; **ADMIN** badge overlays avatar corner (not inline with title); logo, avatar (`sm`), and action icons scale up for the taller toolbar. Desktop keeps single-line title with name + inline admin badge.

**Mobile filter selects:** `ion-select` uses `action-sheet` on mobile viewports (popover clips inside the fixed filter drawer). Helpers: `resolveIonSelectInterface()`, `useIonSelectInterface()`.

## Theme / appearance

**Model:** User preference stored in `localStorage` at `firmshake.themePreference` — `light`, `dark`, or `system` (default).

**Apply:** Ionic `dark.class.css` palette; toggles `ion-palette-dark` on `document.documentElement`. Inline boot script in `index.html` applies stored preference before first paint to avoid flash. `initThemePreferenceOnBoot()` in `main.ts` re-applies and listens to `prefers-color-scheme` when preference is `system`.

**Settings UI:** Settings → **Appearance** segment (Light / Dark / System) on `ProfilePage.vue`.

**Toolbar contrast:** Primary header chrome (`AppTopToolbar`) uses `--fs-toolbar-contrast` (`--ion-color-primary-contrast`). Secondary browse toolbars (`ion-toolbar.app-toolbar-content`) reset `--color` to `--ion-text-color` so filter/search icons stay visible in light mode.

**Implementation:** `themePreference.ts`, `variables.css`, `layout.css`, `ProfilePage.vue`, `index.html`.

## Loading UX

**Tab refresh indicator:** Replace visible "Updating…" copy with a debounced circular spinner centered in the header toolbar. Default **300ms** show delay + **500ms** minimum display via `AppTabRefreshingIndicator` + `useDebouncedVisibility` — avoids flicker on fast refreshes. See **Local-first cached listings** in `firmshake-local-first.mdc`.

**End-of-list copy:** Show "You have reached the bottom of the list!" only when the list is actually scrollable (`isScrollable`: content height exceeds viewport). Prevents orphan footer text on short lists that fit on screen.

**Implementation:** `AppTabRefreshingIndicator.vue`, `useLazyReveal.ts` (`allItemsRevealed` + `isScrollable`), Browse `HomePage.vue`.

## Optimization choices

Reference for performance architecture. Prefer extending these patterns over inventing alternatives unless requirements change.

### Auth / ID token

**Deduped ID token:** `getDedupedIdToken()` coalesces concurrent `getIdToken` calls for the same user/refresh flag, wraps each fetch in a **2s timeout**, and applies a **60s cooldown** before honoring another forced refresh.

**Why:** Login, router guards, API calls, and Firestore probes all need tokens at once; deduping avoids redundant network work and racey refresh storms.

**Two Firestore-auth paths:**
- `waitForFirestoreAuth()` — full path: `authStateReady` → ID token → Firestore probe (`getDoc users/{uid}`) with retries (up to **8s** overall, **3s** per probe). Used before data writes and auth-page redirects.
- `waitForFirestoreAuthNavigation()` — fast path: `authStateReady` + ID token only; skips probe. Used by router guards, bootstrap, and tab prefetch so navigation is not blocked on Firestore propagation.

**Verified-session cache:** Successful auth waits mark the UID verified for **30s** (`AUTH_VERIFIED_TTL_MS`); subsequent waits reuse the cached user. In-flight waits are also deduped per UID.

**Session maintenance:** Proactive token refresh every **12h**, activity-based session extension, and permission-denied → session-expired handling live in `sessionExpiry.ts`. Logout/MFA/user-switch clears token cache via `clearIdTokenCache()` / `clearFirestoreAuthCache()`.

**Tradeoff:** Navigation fast path may reach tab UI before Firestore rules have propagated; tab loaders and `withTransientFirestoreRetry` / `attachRetriableSnapshot` absorb transient permission-denied errors instead of blocking the shell.

**Implementation:** `idToken.ts`, `firestoreAuth.ts`, `sessionExpiry.ts`, `auth.ts`.

### Firestore connection lifecycle

**Reset on session change:** `resetFirestoreConnection()` terminates and recreates Firestore after **logout**, **user switch**, and **MFA login** so IndexedDB persistence leases and cached credentials from the previous session are not reused.

**Multi-tab persistence:** Web uses `persistentMultipleTabManager()`; native uses single-tab cache.

**Retriable reads:** `attachRetriableSnapshot()` and `withTransientFirestoreRetry()` retry permission-denied / timeout errors with backoff while auth propagates, surfacing `SessionExpiredError` only when the session is actually dead.

**Implementation:** `firebase.ts`, `firestoreAuth.ts`, `auth.ts` (logout / MFA / user-switch call sites).

### Tab feeds (stale-while-revalidate)

**SWR cache layer:** `responseCache.ts` — in-memory + `sessionStorage`, **5 min TTL**, `getCached` vs `getStaleCached` (stale allowed for instant paint). `readStaleOnBoot()` hydrates memory from storage before Vue mounts. Per-user keys via `buildUserCacheKey`; `clearCacheIfUserChanged()` invalidates profile/browse/tab namespaces on UID change.

**Tab-specific wrappers:**
- `tabFeedCache.ts` — inbox threads, selling listings
- `browseFeedCache.ts` — browse first page (cursor `lastDoc` not persisted; re-fetched on refresh)

**Loader pattern:** `useTabFeedLoader` — **8s** timeout clears stuck spinners; `hydrateFromCache()` paints stale data immediately (`loading=false`, `refreshing=true`) then live Firestore subscription replaces it. Buying/Inbox/Selling pages use this; Browse hydrates similarly in `HomePage.vue`.

**Background prefetch:** After bootstrap, `scheduleTabPrefetch()` runs on `requestIdleCallback` (1.5s fallback): lazy-imports tab route chunks + skeleton components, then subscribes to inbox threads and seller listings to warm caches. Direct tab URL entry (`bootstrapDirectTabEntry`) prefetches eagerly.

**Tradeoff:** Stale cache may briefly show outdated threads/listings until the live subscription fires; acceptable for perceived speed. Pagination cursors are not cached — load-more always hits the network.

**Implementation:** `responseCache.ts`, `tabFeedCache.ts`, `browseFeedCache.ts`, `useTabFeedLoader.ts`, `tabPrefetch.ts`, tab pages under `features/buying`, `features/selling`, `features/messages`, `HomePage.vue`.

### Boot / startup

**Instant boot shell:** Static HTML/CSS skeleton in `index.html` (`#app-boot-shell`) renders before JS — tab-aware title/header. Removed when `router.isReady()` in `App.vue`. Build-version and stale-chunk handlers reload once per session to recover from deploy mismatches.

**Entry split:** `bootstrap.ts` dynamically imports `main-logs` vs `main` so `/logs` does not load Firebase/auth (avoids competing Firestore IndexedDB leases across tabs).

**Early hydration:** `main.ts` calls `initResponseCacheOnPageLoad()`, `hydrateBootstrapFromCache()`, and `bootstrapDirectTabEntry()` before `app.mount()` so first paint can use cached communities/profile/tab feeds.

**App bootstrap:** `startAppBootstrap()` hydrates communities/profile from stale cache, uses `waitForFirestoreAuthNavigation()` (non-blocking on probe failure), subscribes profile with a **2s fallback** to unblock `bootstrapReady`, refreshes communities in background when cache hit, then schedules tab prefetch. `waitForBootstrap()` caps wait at **4s** with seed fallbacks.

**Deferred router post-auth:** Tab-shell navigation (`shouldDeferPostAuthChecks`) does not block on profile/MFA fetches — shell shows immediately; `scheduleDeferredPostAuthCheck()` verifies in background. Cached profile in router guard skips network when possible. After fresh login, `setPostAuthBypass()` skips repeat checks for **30s**.

**Tradeoff:** User may briefly see a tab before deferred redirect to Complete Profile / MFA enroll; acceptable vs blocking every tab switch on Firestore.

**Implementation:** `index.html`, `bootstrap.ts`, `main.ts`, `App.vue`, `appBootstrap.ts`, `router/index.ts`, `router/tabsRoute.ts`, `auth.ts`.

### Network / data fetching

**Batched listing reads:** `getListingsByIds()` chunks IDs into batches of **30** (Firestore `in` limit), runs batches **in parallel**, and optionally reads from local cache first (`preferCache: true`). Used by thread enrichment and buying/selling/inbox row hydration.

**Thread enrichment:** `enrichThreads()` batch-fetches listing metadata for all threads in one call; on failure emits unenriched threads rather than blocking the list.

**Controlled concurrency:** Thread rebuild uses **5** concurrent workers (`REBUILD_CONCURRENCY`); parallel `Promise.all` for independent queries (e.g. sent/received message snapshots).

**Tradeoff:** Parallel batches increase burst load but cut wall-clock time for enriched lists; prefer batching over N sequential `getDoc` calls.

**Implementation:** `listings.ts`, `threads.ts`, `messages.ts`.

### UI performance

Cross-reference **Loading UX** above for the debounced refresh spinner (**300ms** show delay, **500ms** min display) and scrollability-gated end-of-list copy. Cross-reference **`firmshake-local-first.mdc`** for browse prefetch thresholds and summary caching.

**Lazy reveal / virtualized paint:** `useLazyReveal` renders ~**2× viewport** items initially (`batchSize = itemsPerScreen × 2`), loads more on scroll (**75%** `SCROLL_REVEAL_THRESHOLD`), and enforces a **500ms** minimum skeleton display to avoid flash-of-empty. Trailing row skeletons indicate more items below the fold. Silent feed prefetch at **55%** is handled in `HomePage.vue` (`browseSearchPrefetch.ts`).

**Background refresh vs skeleton:** Cache hydration skips the full-page skeleton (`AppTabLoadingState`) when stale data exists; header `AppTabRefreshingIndicator` signals background revalidation instead.

**Implementation:** `useLazyReveal.ts`, `useDebouncedVisibility.ts`, `AppTabRefreshingIndicator.vue`, `AppTabLoadingState.vue`, list pages (Browse, Buying, Selling, Inbox).

## Spacing & padding

Page inset, section gaps, card grid spacing, sidebar padding, and toolbar margins use shared CSS tokens (`--fs-*`) and layout classes. **Do not** stack `ion-padding` on pages that already wrap content in `AppContentFrame`.

**Implementation:** `src/theme/variables.css`, `src/theme/layout.css`, `AppContentFrame.vue`, `.cursor/rules/firmshake-spacing.mdc`.

## Debug logs & targeted tests

When debugging multi-step features, add **`debugLog`** entries (category + message + data) and inspect via **`/logs`**. Behavior changes require unit tests; run **targeted** specs for touched modules (`npm run test:unit -- --run tests/unit/<spec>.ts`), not always the full suite.

**Implementation:** `src/common/debug/debugLog.ts`, `src/features/debug/views/LogsPage.vue`, `.cursor/rules/firmshake-debug-test.mdc`.

## General data patterns

**Inbox / threads filtering:** Subscribe to full `users/{uid}/inboxState` snapshot; partition threads client-side with `partitionByArchive()`. Acceptable while inbox scale is modest — avoids composite queries and keeps archive/read state co-located per user.

**Key modules:** `inboxState.ts`, `threads.ts`, tab pages under `features/buying`, `features/selling`, `features/messages`.

## Setup & troubleshooting docs

When writing or updating setup, deployment, or troubleshooting docs (`docs/*.md`, README setup sections, `.env.example` comments):

- Include a prominent **"What you need to do"** section near the top (after a one-paragraph summary).
- Use **numbered manual steps** for actions only a human can perform: Firebase Console, Google Cloud Console, Stripe dashboard, DNS, GitHub secrets, etc.
- Make console paths explicit (project name, menu trail) and provide **copy-paste blocks** for URIs, domains, env values, and CLI commands.
- Include **how to verify** (retry flow, check `/logs`, expected headers/responses) and **when to redeploy** (or explicitly "no redeploy needed").
- Do **not** add an empty "What you need to do" section when the doc is purely architectural or client-only with no console steps.

Reference: [`docs/google-sign-in-ux.md`](../../docs/google-sign-in-ux.md), [`docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md`](../../docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md).
